<u>07-SEP-2005 10:41 PM (AUS Time)</u><br>
The goal for today is to visit the Sunshine Coast of Australia, roughly about 1 hr north of Brisbane.  Starting from Hervey Bay we would wind back and forth across the coast and end up eventually down to the Gold Coast. It was going to be a long day of driving and looking.  
<p>
Having driven pass the famous big pineapple (I don't really know if it has any purpose other than to just sit there and take photographs in front of), our first stop would be the city of Eumundi where a famous marketplace occurs on Wednesdays and Saturdays only.  We didn't plan it but it just worked out this way that today was Wednesday.  As soon as we hit the town of Eumundi, we encountered much traffic congestion and parking problems.  But there was the market.  Crowded as ever.  A large gravel parking existed right after the marketplace so we parked there and walked into the market.  Very much similar to the Portland Saturday Market, the local area artisans were selling their crafts as well as food and music being performed.  
<p>
<!--
<img src=http://www.mybigadventure.com/ankesh/picupload/Uploads/Images/1126439060_2.jpg>-->
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=../picupload/Uploads/Images/1126439060_2.jpg"><img src="picupload/Uploads/Images/Small/1126439060_2.jpg"></a>
<p>
Having had our share of the Eumundi marketplace, we drove out to Noosa Heads.  Noosa is a famous touristy town known for it's main beach called Noosa Main Beach (how obvious :) ). Sprawling with hundreds of people included some surfers but mostly sunbathers and kids would like to play in the water, it looked like a fun place to get a tan (if we really needed one).  M and I decided to head up to the Noosa National Park instead.  We hiked along the ocean shores up to Teatree Beach and turned around.  Gorgeous rocky beaches.  On my way out, I had to run to the bathroom and nearly missed a monitor lizard walking around right next to me.  Luckily, M told me to watch out and I pulled out the camera to take a few pics. I'd seem them at the zoo before but never out in the wild.
<p>
<!--
<img src=http://www.mybigadventure.com/ankesh/picupload/Uploads/Images/1126439060_3.jpg>-->
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=../picupload/Uploads/Images/1126439060_3.jpg"><img src="picupload/Uploads/Images/Small/1126439060_3.jpg"></a>
